    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "“Cloonlara”                                    \r\nDowth, Co Meath.   A92E702\r\nA fine 4 Bed Detached Home in a beautiful country setting.\r\n\r\nLOCATION:\r\nEircode is: A92 E702           Folio. MH 26746\r\n\r\n\"Cloonlara\" is a beautiful four-bedroom detached property, surrounded by picturesque gardens and mature landscaping. Ideally located on a well-maintained site that extends to approximately 0.16 Hectares (0.4 of an acre), this spacious house offers a purchaser an ideal private family home in a tranquil setting. \r\n\r\nCloonlara strikes the perfect balance between peaceful rural living and convenient access to local amenities. The property is situated in the UNESCO World Heritage Site of Brú na Bóinne, which includes the famous archaeological sites of Newgrange, Knowth, and Dowth. This area of the Boyne Valley is highly regarded and is near impossible to achieve planning permission in the area. \r\nWith its generous accommodations, appealing grounds, and idyllic rural setting, Cloonlara presents an excellent \r\nopportunity to enjoy a relaxed country lifestyle in an area rich in history and natural beauty.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION:\r\nThe well-designed accommodation features a welcoming entrance hall, an inner reception room/ bedroom, a dining room, a spacious kitchen with open access to the dining area, a wonderful bright sunroom located just off the living room, an ideal location to enjoy your morning coffee. The property includes an upstairs attic room, along with additional attic space. Bedrooms 2, 3 & 4 are all generously proportioned, while the wet room adds practicality and convenience. In addition to the separate WC/ shower the property also benefits from a garage, providing valuable additional storage and large driveway and EV charger.\r\nOutside, the attractive gazebo and decking areas create a perfect outdoor dining room for al fresco dining and entertaining. The gardens offer a sense of privacy, with secluded alcoves and thoughtfully divided side and rear gardens creating a variety of private areas. \r\n“Cloonlara” has been constantly upgraded and extended over the years, resulting in a beautiful, easy-flowing living space."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "ACCOMMODATION: \r\n\r\nSummary: The property offers generously proportioned living areas that are filled with natural light. \r\n \r\nHallway 1.68m x 3.67m – 6.85m x 1.28m: Wooden flooring, with access to inner reception room/bedroom and wetroom. \r\n\r\nLivingroom: 7.69m x 4.04m : carpet, fireplace, recessed lights, built-in shelving.\r\n\r\nSunroom: 3.93m x 4.05m: Wooden ceiling feature, recessed lights, Tiled floor, windows on all sides.\r\n\r\nKitchen: 3.79m x 4.15m: Built-in units, tiled floor, tiled splashback, arch to dining area\r\n\r\nDining room: 3.79 x 3.53m: wooden ceiling feature\r\n\r\nHall - Stairs: Carpet.\r\n\r\nFamily room: 3.27 x 3.06m :\r\n\r\nBathroom: 1.39m x 2.83m : WC, WHB, shower, tiled floor to ceiling.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1: 3.55m x 3.57m: wooden flooring, built-in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2: 3.84m x 4.37m: wooden flooring, built-in wardrobes\r\n\r\nBedroom 3: 3.62m x 3.96m: wooden flooring, built-in wardrobes\r\n\r\nMain Bathroom / Wetroom: 1.82m x 2.65m: WC, WHB, shower, tiled floor to ceiling.\r\n\r\nInner reception room/bedroom 4: 3.82m x 3.55m: wooden flooring, built in wardrobes\r\n\r\nHotpress: Storage \r\n\r\n2nd Floor\r\nAttic room: 3.16m x 5.78m: wooden flooring, Velux window.\r\n\r\nAdditional Attic/storage room: 3.16m x 4.29m"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Features:\r\n•\tAn idyllic 4-bedroom detached family home, perfect for modern living\r\n\r\n•\tFloor Area Nett Internal Floor Area 183m² (1,970 ft²) excludes attic, low ceilings, walls)\r\n\r\n•\tAn oasis of peace and tranquility, yet at the edge of all the amenities that The Boyne Valley has to offer.\r\n\r\n•\tModern open-plan kitchen nicely flows into the adjoining living room. \r\n\r\n•\tRelaxing Sunroom. Outdoor Gazebo with decking.\r\n\r\n•\tWithin  the UNESCO World Heritage Site of Brú na Bóinne\r\n\r\n•\tWithin easy reach of renowned primary & secondary schools, close to all amenities\r\n\r\n•\tConveniently located close to M1 motorway,N2,Drogheda train station and Dublin Airport\r\n\r\n•\tMains electricity, mains water.  Heating oil-fired boiler. Fiber broadband.\r\n\r\n•\tEV, electric charging point outside.\r\n\r\n•\tGarage\r\n\r\n•\tTenure – Freehold \r\n\r\n•\tBER:\r\nBER Rating C      BER Number 119702397"
